   "tests": [
  {
   "id": "staggered_operators_initial",
   "description": "Pins the staggered-grid discrete operators pointwise at the initial state (t = 0): Wstag (mask-aware edge averaging, water_thickness_staggered), Kstag (Mahaffy-like Pi of the reduced potential R = P_over + rho_w g b and the conductivity k Wstag^(alpha-1) (Pi + eps^2)^((beta-2)/2), eps = 1), Vstag (edge velocity -K grad R with the Wstag > 0 guard), and Qstag (first-order upwind V W_upwind) at interior staggered points (o = 1 east edge, o = 2 north edge of the cell), plus R and the grounded mask. The expected values are computed from the C++ formulas of Routing.cc (water_thickness_staggered, compute_conductivity, compute_velocity, advective_fluxes) applied to the dumped initial field W_in and geometry: the dump's staggered.csv samples the LAST internal substep, which the continuous trajectory does not reproduce pointwise, so the initial state is the honest pinning target for the operators (the o = 1/2 east/north mapping, the Mahaffy stencils, the mask branches, and the upwind direction). rel 1e-12: the esm evaluates the same formulas in f64 (cross-language pow() ulps ~1e-16).",
   "time_span": {
    "start": 0.0,
    "end": 0.0
   },
   "assertions": [
    {
     "variable": "Wstag",
     "time": 0.0,
     "coords": {
